Confirming this bug is still active on **v1.15.10** (latest release, 2026-05-23). The 2026 reproduction below adds production-grade evidence to the original 2025 v1.2.21 trace.

## Reproduction on v1.15.10

I'm running `opencode acp` as a subprocess over stdio under a custom ACP client. All LLM traffic is routed through a local LiteLLM proxy so canonical request/response payloads are persisted and queryable post-mortem.

Prompt: *"list the files under /home with bash ls, then reply in one sentence describing what you found"* against `openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash`. Turn fires two LLM round-trips (tool-call → bash ls → final text reply).

### Canonical model output (read from `LiteLLM_SpendLogs.response`)

```json
"choices": [{
  "message": {
    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "There is only one user directory in /home: `agent`.",
    "reasoning_content": "...",
    "tool_calls": null
  },
  "finish_reason": "stop"
}]
```

### What the ACP client observed
**Empty visible reply.** The final `agent_message_chunk` for the post-tool-call text part lands after the `session/prompt` RPC response with `stopReason: "end_turn"`, identical to the symptom @hancengiz reported in this issue. Linked PR #21316 by @LydiaCai1203 traced the same root cause: in `packages/opencode/src/acp/agent.ts:prompt`, the awaited `session.prompt` RPC returns while the SSE delta subscription is still draining text-delta events for that message — those late deltas reach `connection.sessionUpdate(...)` after the RPC reply has already gone out.

## PR #21316 was auto-closed before review

[#21316](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/21316) ("fix(acp): serialize session updates to prevent out-of-order messages") implemented both halves of a canonical fix:

1. **Serialized `sendChain`** — all `sessionUpdate` calls go through a single promise chain, guaranteeing in-order delivery.
2. **`reconcileAssistantMessage()`** — after `prompt()` returns, fetch the canonical assistant message via REST and replay any text/reasoning content the delta stream missed.

It was auto-closed by the github-actions compliance bot two hours after filing for an incomplete PR description template — never reviewed on the merits. Reopening it (or asking @LydiaCai1203 to resubmit with the template filled in) would close this issue with code that's already written.

## Proposed fix (sketch for `packages/opencode/src/acp/agent.ts`)

If #21316 isn't revivable, the reconciliation half can be re-derived in ~30 LOC against current `agent.ts`. The shape:

